 SAP Document AI basic UI.       When you upload a document and choose it on the Documents screen, you now see the extraction results for header fields and line items alongside the document preview, without first having to click Extraction Results.      In the extraction results, you can now use the filters at the top of the Edit pane to set which extraction confidence ranges to display. You can select either a single range or all of them.      When using the Template feature, you can now edit and confirm extraction results for the associated document by choosing it on the details page for the template you've created.      Also on the Template details page, you can now set an extraction method for individual fields or for all fields your template. The available methods are Template and AI.      See View and Edit Extraction Results, Add Documents and Activate/Deactivate Template, and Add Template.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-08\nValid as Of: 2024-10-08\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2146 ---\nComponent: SAP Document AI\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Factur-X and ZUGFeRD Standards - Support for Version 2.3\nDescription: SAP Document AI now supports the version 2.3 of e-invoice document files in Factur-X and ZUGFeRD standards.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-08\nValid as Of: 2024-10-08\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2147 ---\nComponent: SAP Document AI\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Instant Learning for Information Extraction Using Generative AI (Premium Edition)\nDescription: SAP Document AI now allows you to enhance extraction with generative AI by using your edited extraction results to enrich the prompt to large language models (LLMs) with user feedback.  If you use an appropriately configured schema, SAP Document AI learns from your feedback 